  "response_text": "The way our stack allocation method works is by taking an initial value for the beginning of our stack, MSP_init_val and beginning with our main stack. This main stack houses our setup and other OS-specific things required for the program to run. Below that are the stacks that we allocate ourselves. For example if we wanted our main stack to be 0x600 bytes, we would start our first thread at MSP_init_val \u2013 0x600 since our stack grows downwards and we are now giving the main stack 0x600 bytes of space. This stack allocation method is why we needed MSP_init_val to get a new value for PSP_val. Without MSP_init_val, we could not ensure the size of our main stack.\\n",
